<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Styria</h1><p class="st-meta">1180 CE – 1918 CE · capital Graz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alpine duchy of Graz and the Erzberg iron mountain, a Habsburg land for over six centuries and the shield of Inner Austria against the Ottomans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The March of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> grew from a Carolingian border zone ruled from the 11th century by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otakars">Otakar</a> counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steyr">Steyr</a>. In 1180 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Emperor Frederick Barbarossa</a> raised it to a duchy for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-iv-of-styria">Ottokar IV</a>. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgenberg-pact">Georgenberg Pact</a> of 1186 it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-babenberg">Babenbergs</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-austria">Duchy of Austria</a> in 1192, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a> it came to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1282.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> was governed by its dukes with strong estates meeting in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landhaus-graz">Landhaus</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graz">Graz</a>. Iron from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzberg">Erzberg</a> made it an industrial heartland. From 1564 Graz was capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/inner-austria">Inner Austria</a> under Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-archduke-of-austria">Charles II</a>, who invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>; his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand II</a> expelled Protestants. Repeated Ottoman raids made defence a constant concern. German was spoken in the north and Slovene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-styria">Lower Styria</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> remained a crown land of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> until 1918. It was then divided: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-styria">Lower Styria</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maribor">Maribor</a> went to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes</a> and is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, while the rest became the Austrian state of Styria.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-styria.jpg" alt="Duchy of Styria" width="320" height="199"><figcaption>Image: Theodore Christopher The SVG code is valid. This vector image was created with a text editor. The drawing is extremel... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Styria_Flag_until_1960.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1180 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Graz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ottokar IV, Charles II of Inner Austria, Ferdinand II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Slovene</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/slovenia">Slovenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Herzogtum Steiermark</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1549&amp;focus=duchy-of-styria" aria-label="Duchy of Styria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5042 525 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Styria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" wid